{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-40382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ then $z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-40382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/assets/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot (-1)+6\\cdot 4}{{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{30+3+3+24}{36+9+9+36}a \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{90}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-40382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b582ab2645b673422a1d694273fccf4a79b63fb29223ea8da4cde7b2d6508828"} {"question" "q-40382" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-40382" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$-"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-40382" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-40411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $x$ and $\\text{Span}{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-40411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The distance between the vector $x$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by $‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{x}$ in the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{span}{b}.$\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{b\\cdot x}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-2)+(-1)(-2)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2-2+2}{1+1+1+1}b \\\\  & =-b \\\\  & =-1[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{((-2)-(-1))^{2}+(2-1)^{2}+((-2)-(-1))^{2}+((-2)-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-40411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b582ab2645b673422a1d694273fccf4a79b63fb29223ea8da4cde7b2d6508828"} {"question" "q-40411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-40411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-40411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-81201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $x$ and the system of  linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-81201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=3{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{10}b \\\\  & =b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-81201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b582ab2645b673422a1d694273fccf4a79b63fb29223ea8da4cde7b2d6508828"} {"question" "q-81201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-81201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-81201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-140116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $x$ and $\\text{Span}{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-140116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The distance between the vector $x$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by $‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{x}$ in the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{span}{b}.$\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{b\\cdot x}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot (-2)}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{6+4+2}{4+1+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-4)^{2}+(4-2)^{2}+(-2-(-2))^{2}+(-2-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+0+4} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-140116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b582ab2645b673422a1d694273fccf4a79b63fb29223ea8da4cde7b2d6508828"} {"question" "q-140116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-140116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-140116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-140118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-140118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-3{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)\\cdot (-3)+8\\cdot 1}{{(-3)}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{10}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-140118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b582ab2645b673422a1d694273fccf4a79b63fb29223ea8da4cde7b2d6508828"} {"question" "q-140118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-140118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"} {"question" "q-140118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072287/state.json" "file_sha256" "cc6b225e000e359800c6ce4c9079ea4c4d5730c93de3fdcf12b95c99947143b2"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2627 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
